<title>USA: AlliedSignal may cut up to 700 jobs at DOE plant.</title>
<headline>AlliedSignal may cut up to 700 jobs at DOE plant.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>AlliedSignal Inc may cut as many as 700 jobs in a restructuring move at a plant it operates for the Department of Energy (DOE), a spokeswoman said Thursday.</p>
<p>The Kansas City plant, which is operated by AlliedSignal Federal Manufacturing &amp; Technologies, a unit of AlliedSignal, makes and purchases non-nuclear components for the nuclear weapons complex. AlliedSignal is a prime DOE contractor.</p>
<p>&quot;We will begin a voluntary reduction in force probably sometime later this summer. Following the voluntary reduction in force, it's likely that we will have an involuntary reduction,&quot; said Jane Jankowski, a plant spokeswoman.</p>
<p>((-- Greg Frost, Kansas City bureau, 816 561-8671))</p>
